<https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns/mutation/8636919f-359f-4d27-b758-8dc76144dd54> <https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns#seq> "3750"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns/meta> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns/mutation/8636919f-359f-4d27-b758-8dc76144dd54> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns#Mutation> <https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns/meta> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#basedOnApprovedResult> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/result/VGR-012> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#rationale> "Canonical opening for any verification graph that needs an initialised orchestration store. Step 0 runs `dec init --template engineering-development` (the only way `dec init` succeeds without a Turtle definition file in scope); Step 1 then introspects via a stable subcommand like `dec doctor --format json`. Use this pattern whenever a TC requires verifying anything about the post-init store state." <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#patternName> "init-then-introspect" <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#appliesToSafetyClass> "isolated" <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#exemplarOf> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/VG-005> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/ex/EX-INIT-DOCTOR> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#ExemplarGraph> <https://decision-cli.dev/ns/graph/catalog> .
